    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34233" root="فغر" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ وَاسِعُ فَغْرِ الفَمِ</span></b>  <i>He is wide in the opening of
the mouth.</i> (Lth, O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And accord. to Lth,
(O,) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَغَرٌ</span> signifies also <i>A rose when it opens:</i> (O,
K:) but it is thought by Az to be, in this sense,
a mistake for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَغْوٌ</span>, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span>. (O.)

